  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In a group of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math>&nbsp;persons&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>75</mn></math>&nbsp;speak English and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn></math>&nbsp;speak Hindi. Each person speaks at least one of the two languages. If the number of persons who speak only English is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;and the number of persons who speaks only Hindi is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>, then the eccentricity of the ellipse&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is</p>"
  },
